# VVDN -- 3 synthetic departures in trail from real Gate 26, RWY 35R,
# real SID BUNTA 2G -- companion file to VVDN_DOTEN_3ACFT_TROMBONE_ILSV35L.scn
# (the 3-aircraft ARRIVAL scenario) and built directly from
# VVDN_GATE26_DEP_RWY35R_BUNTA2G.scn (the single-aircraft DEPARTURE
# scenario), per explicit request to combine the two and sequence 3
# departures with continuous 3-minute separation. Callsigns VDN701/702/703
# are SYNTHETIC (not real ADS-B flights).
#
# HOW THE 3-MINUTE SEPARATION IS ENFORCED -- measured from when the
# PRECEDING aircraft begins its takeoff roll to when the NEXT aircraft
# begins its takeoff roll (per the request), NOT from pushback or CRE time:
# all 3 aircraft fly the byte-for-byte IDENTICAL pushback/taxi/hold/roll/
# climb profile from VVDN_GATE26_DEP_RWY35R_BUNTA2G.scn (same gate, same
# taxi route, same speeds), so each aircraft's own ground-transit duration
# from pushback to "lined up and stopped on RWY 35R" is fixed at exactly
# 648.34s, plus the ~5s hold = 653.34s before its takeoff roll begins.
# Because this duration is identical for all 3, staggering each aircraft's
# ENTIRE timeline (CRE + every subsequent command) by a constant +180s
# (3 min) automatically staggers its takeoff-roll-start moment by the same
# +180s -- verified arithmetically before writing this file:
#   VDN701 CRE @ 00:00:00 -> takeoff roll begins @ 00:10:53.34
#   VDN702 CRE @ 00:03:00 -> takeoff roll begins @ 00:13:53.34  (+180.0s)
#   VDN703 CRE @ 00:06:00 -> takeoff roll begins @ 00:16:53.34  (+180.0s)
# This represents ATC metering pushback/taxi clearances 3 minutes apart for
# a gate that turns over 3 flights in a row -- since VDN701 has already
# cleared the ramp/taxiway well before VDN702 pushes back (the taxi-out
# alone takes ~11 min, so by minute 3 VDN701 is already 3 minutes into its
# own taxi, well clear of the gate stand), this is operationally realistic,
# matching the same "identical route, fixed CRE offset" convention already
# used for the 3-aircraft ARRIVAL scenario this file is paired with.
#
# GROUND ROUTE / TAKEOFF ROLL / CLIMB-OUT / SID / PERFORMANCE-MODEL notes
# below are copied verbatim from VVDN_GATE26_DEP_RWY35R_BUNTA2G.scn (the
# single-aircraft version this file was generated from) -- they apply
# identically to all 3 aircraft here, only the callsign and the timestamp
# of every line differ (by the fixed 0s / +180s / +360s offsets above).
#
# NOTE ON "GATE 26": VDN601 in the ARRIVAL reference file actually parks at
# real Gate 24 (16.05337,108.20189, per its own last ADDWPT and
# gates.geojson), not Gate 26 -- flagged honestly, since this file follows
# the gate explicitly named in the original request.
#
# GROUND ROUTE -- every point cross-checked against the real taxiway
# centerlines in FTS Server/data/aerodrome_layout/datasets/vietnam_kml_layout/
# normalized/airports/VVDN/taxiway_centerlines.geojson (all within ~3-25m of
# a real centerline vertex):
#  - Start point = real Gate 26 stand, 16.05262199,108.2019728 (gates.geojson).
#  - Pushback-complete point 16.0524,108.2005 (real bearing 261.1 deg from
#    Gate 26, close to the requested 263 deg nose heading).
#  - Hold-heading-172 taxi to 16.0297,108.2038 (real bearing 172.0 deg).
#  - Turn right to 16.0292,108.2029 (real bearing 240 deg).
#  - Turn right to 16.0295,108.2026 (real bearing 316 deg).
#  - Stop ~5s on RWY 35R at 16.0300,108.2024, ~108m north of the real RWY
#    35R threshold (16.02904,108.20253, runway_centerlines.geojson
#    "17L/35R"). Real RWY 17L/35R centerline: 108.19800,16.06037 (17L end)
#    <-> 108.20253,16.02904 (35R end/threshold), length ~1.90NM.
#
# TAKEOFF ROLL / LIFTOFF POINT (16.062960,108.197580): NOT charted -- 2.0NM
# along the runway heading (352 deg) from the lineup point, same convention
# as BlueSky's own internal "ADDWPT TAKEOFF" special case (route.py's
# addwptStack()). Speed ramps 0->170kt as sqrt(distance); altitude stays 0
# until the last 40% of the roll then climbs to 500ft.
#
# CLIMB-OUT / SID -- real AIP Vietnam "STANDARD DEPARTURE CHART -
# INSTRUMENT (SID) - ICAO, DA NANG/DA NANG INTL (VVDN), RNAV RWY 35L/R"
# (AD 2-VVDN-9-6, AMDT 01/23), BUNTA 2G DEPARTURE:
#   010 CF DN456  crs 360(359T)            alt -2450m(8038ft)
#   020 TF HOKIN   crs 074(072.5T) 43.23km  alt -FL110(11000ft)
#   030 TF BINKU   crs 075(074.0T) 43.79km  alt (none charted)
#   040 TF BUNTA   crs 057(056.0T) 54.24km  alt (none charted)
# DN456/HOKIN altitudes and all 4 waypoints' courses/distances/coordinates
# are real (chart's own WGS-84 list); BINKU/BUNTA altitudes (19000/24000ft)
# and every climb speed are an assumed continued-climb schedule (no real
# chart data for those), flagged honestly as such.
#
# GROUND-SPEED / PERFORMANCE-MODEL LIMITATIONS (carried over from the
# single-aircraft file, apply identically here):
#  - Every commanded speed is EXACTLY 0 (a true stop) or >=4kt -- BlueSky's
#    CAS/Mach ambiguity heuristic (bluesky/tools/aero.py, vcasormach():
#    "ismach = 0.1 < spd < casmach_thr(=2.0 m/s)") misreads any nonzero
#    speed under ~3.9kt as a Mach number, producing a bogus ~650-680kt
#    "aircraft rockets into the sky" bug -- confirmed live and root-caused
#    earlier this session. The originally-requested 2kt pushback speed is
#    therefore floored to 4kt.
#  - This file uses plain MOVE commands (direct lat/lon/alt/hdg/spd
#    assignment every few seconds), not BlueSky's ADDWPT/LNAV/VNAV/route
#    engine, after 3 autopilot-driven attempts each failed live testing
#    with the same overspeed bug. The acceleration/climb profile is
#    therefore this session's own physics approximation (constant-
#    acceleration-equivalent takeoff roll, linear climb rate per leg), NOT
#    the aircraft's real thrust/drag envelope or any BlueSky performance
#    model's output -- even though real BADA v3.16 B738 data is now loaded
#    and selectable via "PERF BADA" in this build (fixed earlier this
#    session by copying bluesky/data/performance/bada/*.OPF/.APF into
#    bluesky/resources/performance/BADA/, the path the engine actually
#    reads from), it is not used by this MOVE-based file.

00:00:00.00>TRAILS ON
00:00:00.00>ASAS ON

00:00:00.00>TRAILS ON
00:00:00.00>ASAS ON

